  "problem": "Historical WP11 v1.3 approval was being checked against current tree bytes except two named package transitions. That first-fails on extra current files such as the 11 PR-005 UI/core inputs, and cannot prove the original 154 sealed preimages offline. Current technical checks still need to run on actual current files without transferring historical approval or silently allowlisting changed product inputs.",
  "resulting_behavior": "The original 154 WP11 v1.3 input preimages (1,347,732 bytes) from 30fa0c59ecd4d3d1dd1f56cd8422c6c470e45cb0 are retained in a portable content-addressed snapshot and verified against sealed receipt e596e1b18a0251f611990c9752e1d12fb36cd05dab16bf55cf96e8d1fc431f9d and historical subject 294d8b40bb5a2dbe1f55cdfde4a60205de75ee1ffe48e0108eae69aea2db0f98 without Git or network. Current technical evidence is built from actual current files and remains pending_authorized_review with approval=null (subject 7e355d27a6deb558b6626c486472763a7cfd61239e054d16e13256162de3829f). The wrapper subject 87fb320c9f415322f52581f3416ac760a58da684bdafd4592bac909bf182115a binds adapter, tests, policy, unchanged runner, snapshot, and reader and is also unapproved. Complete current-versus-historical reporting lists every changed sealed input: two package transitions on this integration tree, 13 on original PR-005 941c9cd. Direct --validate/--issue still reject historical approval on the current subject. This is not combined PR005/PR086 acceptance or release qualification.",
